{"term":"slip","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:2ae8a3b536bcc9e4cb","definition":"To lose one’s traction on a slippery surface; to slide due to a lack of friction.","example":"[...] but in the damp conditions prevailing the driver sensibly was unwilling to attempt the climb up through Combe Down tunnel without help, for fear of slipping to a standstill in the unventilated bore, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slip#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:84650734829cefad2f","definition":"To err.","example":"There is one that slippeth in his speach, but not from his heart, and who is he that hath not offended with his tongue?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slip#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8bad13dfe1e88879b9","definition":"To accidentally reveal a secret or otherwise say something unintentionally.","example":"She kept engaging with the caller, though, hoping he would slip and reveal her daughter’s location.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slip#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b4559b613e22f7398c","definition":"To move or fly (out of place); to shoot; often with out, off, etc.","example":"A bone may slip out of place.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"